ld not be in english for  a lot of the world and uh and we we've  had  methods of sort of doing this in the  past um but it was sort of clunky and it  made it difficult for the translators  to translate the text which is a problem  because if it's difficult for the  translators then it doesn't happen as  much and then  it doesn't look as good and stuff so um  trying to sort of ease the transition  for everybody and make it easier to  get our content translated which is good  and you know just to take a step back  you mentioned you interned here twice  um what what brought you to khan academy  i guess as an intern but then eventually  as a full-time engineer um originally  well uh  back to ben albert uh ben alpert was an  intern here before me and i knew him  back from high school and uh sounded  like fun but also um i've been really  interested in education  um and stuff throughout my life i really  like  teaching people things and i worked as  like a  ta in college a bunch and so i  thought about it and thought like you  know a place that does online education  sounds really fun and uh  i um  looked on  the website and  uh i checked out like the con exercises  stuff that we had been going on and saw  that you know people were just writing  really cool problems um for students to  solve and writing uh coming up with  hints to like that we're really good at  explaining exactly how the students  should go through this and i thought  that this was a really cool way to  further education so and since interning  twice and then now being a full-time  engineer what's kind of surprised you  about khan academy  i think the biggest surprise is how  nice the people are i think that  the the sort of the culture that khan  academy creates  with people are very passionate about  the stuff that we do  um we're not we're not in it for the  money or whatever we're here because we  we really care about changing education  and the work that we're doing and so  everyone that ends up he